# Story page: classic
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Old Yard
---
Past the hedge lies the Old Yard, ringed by red walls that have stood for a thousand years and have every intention of standing for a thousand more.

{name} bumped one. The wall did not apologize. Walls never do, which is the principal reason I avoid them, along with dinner parties.

Carved into one brick was a snake devouring its own tail, an image the learned call an ouroboros and everyone else calls a bad sign.
